      },
      {
        order = 4,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "Enemies in Promyvion are called \"The Empty\". Each Promyvion has 4 different kinds of Empty: Wanderers, Weepers, Seethers, and a final type that is exclusive to each Promyvion. The monsters have a level range depending on islands like so:",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Promyvion" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 5,
        marker = "**",
        depth = 2,
        instruction = "1st: Easy Prey to Decent Challenge to level 30",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Easy Prey", "Decent Challenge" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 6,
        marker = "**",
        depth = 2,
        instruction = "2nd: Even Match to Tough to level 30",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Even Match", "Tough" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 7,
        marker = "**",
        depth = 2,
        instruction = "3rd (note that there are two possible third islands, and the one you get warped to varies by Memory Stream): Very Tough to Incredibly Tough to level 30",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Very Tough", "Incredibly Tough" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 8,
        marker = "**",
        depth = 2,
        instruction = "4th: Incredibly Tough++ to level 30",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Incredibly Tough" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 9,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "New Apex monsters, added in November 2021, can easily aggro and kill even a level 99 player if caught unprepared. However, they are usually easy to avoid.",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 10,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "All monsters are Too Weak to a level 75 character, except for Apex monsters, which can be easily avoided on the way to the battlefields.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Too Weak" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 11,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "Weepers and Wanderers are the weakest monster types, besides Strays.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Stray" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 12,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "Do not bother with Sneak or Invisible, because all monsters on all islands are True Sight and aggressive, but only enemies with similar elemental cores will link. Per usual, monsters that check as too weak will not aggro.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Sneak", "Invisible", "True Sight" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 13,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "Section: General Information.",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 14,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "Buffs no longer wear off when entering Promyvion. Maps on this site show the locations of all the Memory Receptacles and teleport locations.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Memory Receptacle" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 15,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "To proceed to the next island in the sequence, you must find and defeat a Memory Receptacle. They appear on teleport platforms found on each island. There are several possible locations on the second and third islands. The locations of those Memory Receptacles is random. Receptacles spawn several Strays. If the Memory Receptacle is real, a Memory Stream appears upon... Required details: Memory Receptacle, Stray.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Memory Receptacle", "Stray" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 16,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "If you need to return to a previous island, search for a platform that has a live portal, but no Memory Receptacle in it. That is the portal back.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Memory Receptacle" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 17,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "On the final island, there is no Memory Receptacle, but a zoneline to the Spire (battlefield entrance). It may be very difficult to avoid aggro on the fourth floor if you have no high level players to clear the path, but if you get caught and the castle-like structure is nearby, you should be able to zone easily.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Memory Receptacle" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 18,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "If using anima in a party, you may want to agree on an order of use for anima. They last 30 seconds and overlap (using one during the effect of another of the same type resets the duration to 30 seconds), but panicking and using three at once is a waste. Also note that the effects of anima stack, so you can use Psychoanima and Hysteroanima in pairs to stop all attacks.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "anima", "Psychoanima", "Hysteroanima" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
